## Building a Text Adventure Room

### Defining Game Elements

```xiom
enum Direction {
  North;
  South;
  East;
  West;
}

type Room {
  description: Str;
  has_chest: Bool;
  chest_open: Bool;
  has_key: Bool;
  has_exit: Bool;
}

type Player {
  has_key: Bool;
  position: Str;
}
```

### Room Description

```xiom
fn describe_room(room: &Room) -> Str {
  let mut desc = "You are in a dimly lit stone chamber.";

  if room.has_chest && !room.chest_open {
    desc = string.str_concat(desc, " There is a wooden chest here.");
  };
  if room.has_chest && room.chest_open && room.has_key {
    desc = string.str_concat(desc, " The chest is open and contains a rusty key.");
  };
  if room.has_exit {
    desc = string.str_concat(desc, " A door leads north.");
  };
  desc
}
```

### Processing Commands

```xiom
fn process_command(command: Str, room: &mut Room, player: &mut Player) -> Str {
  if command == "look" {
    return describe_room(room);
  };
  if command == "open chest" && room.has_chest && !room.chest_open {
    room.chest_open = true;
    return "You open the chest. Inside is a rusty key.";
  };
  if command == "take key" && room.chest_open && room.has_key && !player.has_key {
    player.has_key = true;
    room.has_key = false;
    return "You take the key.";
  };
  if command == "go north" && player.has_key && room.has_exit {
    return "You unlock the door and escape! YOU WIN!";
  };
  "You can't do that."
}
```

### The Game Loop

```xiom
fn play_game() {
  let mut room = Room{ description: "...", has_chest: true, chest_open: false, has_key: true, has_exit: true };
  let mut player = Player{ has_key: false, position: "room" };
  io.println(describe_room(&room));
  io.println(process_command("open chest", &mut room, &mut player));
  io.println(process_command("take key", &mut room, &mut player));
  io.println(process_command("go north", &mut room, &mut player));
}
```

